    "proof_outline": [
      "Even2m: a shortest m+1-point block must contain an adjacent pair in every path; alternating high0,low0,high1,low1,... attains that bound.",
      "Odd2m+1: avoiding internal edges of two distinct m+1-point blocks would force their intersection to use only the complement of their union. The intersection has one more point than that complement, which traps the full path there and excludes the symmetric difference. Thus the second-shortest block width is an upper bound.",
      "Rotate labels so a shortest m+1-point block comes first, then take0,m+1,1,m+2,...,m. Every edge spans at least m index steps on the line and avoids the shortest block internally, attaining the second-smallest width."
